      "box": [
        72.0,
        569.314697265625,
        520.8220825195312,
        667.5526123046875
      ],
      "text": "Kākāpō are solitary birds and tend to occupy the same home range for many\nyears. They forage on the ground and climb high into trees. They often leap\nfrom trees and flap their wings, but at best manage a controlled descent to the\nground. They are entirely vegetarian, with their diet including the leaves, roots\nand bark of trees as well as bulbs, and fern fronds.\n"
    },
